FAISS DB + PDFs Sizing (Scenario Summary)
Scenario
- Clients: 5,000
- Docs/client: 20 → PDFs total: 100,000
- Pages/PDF: 100
- Chunks/page: 1.5 → Vectors total: 15,000,000
Assumptions
- FAISS IndexFlat, embeddings D=1024, float32
- LangChain metadata ≈ 400 B/chunk
- Per-client indexes on disk; loaded via LRU MAX_LOADED
- Average PDF sizes shown at 1.5 MB and 5 MB for range
Bottom line
Disk — FAISS (all clients): ~63 GiB
- ~57.2 GiB vectors
- ~5.6 GiB metadata
- Small IDs/aux = index IDs (int64) + pickle overhead, ~0.1–0.2 GiB

Disk — PDFs (all):
- ~150 GB @ 1.5 MB/PDF
- ~500 GB @ 5 MB/PDF

RAM — FAISS (by MAX_LOADED):
(MAX_LOADED = how many client FAISS indexes are kept hot in memory at once; others are evicted and reloaded on demand.)
MAX_LOADED	Approx FAISS RAM
5	~70–100 MiB
10	~130–180 MiB
25	~325–450 MiB
